            "Concentration of total trihalomethane in drinking water. Disinfection by-products are chemicals that form when a disinfectant like chlorine reacts with naturally occurring organic matter and other substances in the source water. Current research is investigating whether there are health effects from chronic exposure to the by-products of water disinfection.",
            "Nitrate",
            "Concentration of nitrate in drinking water. Nitrates are found in water near where nitrogen-based fertilizers are used. Infants who are fed formula made with water containing nitrates over 10 mg/L sometimes became seriously ill.",
